  "behavior": [
    "Native execution and private NN workspace tracing share one contiguous-then-independent-copy program, retaining intermediate descriptors before fallible work.",
    "Move-only sealed plans validate exact imported source roots and capacities, isolate tracing from caller mutation, retain all destination overlap, reject aliasing outputs, and preserve typed overflow and incomplete facts.",
    "Runtime binds the original source-selection token to an existing-only registry witness; source-origin health and destination capacity are checked in one existing-ledger transaction.",
    "Copy accounts expose one work scope and closed destination custody, without inference geometry or future run/scope grants. Source pins retire only at certification or remain quarantined.",
    "Native key/scalar copying checks the original funded sampler, exact current request/frontier/epoch/revision and completed pending receipt, retaining one submission lease through inspection, admission and copying.",
    "Only final copied backings are published after exact native settlement. Source/model arrays are excluded from destination publication; partial sources/intermediates remain under recovery.",
    "Settled read-only worker failure preserves source usability. Early and late native recovery failures still fence the session while retaining the original typed worker error.",
    "Saved numerical arrays and escaped raw aliases remain independently charged after source/model retirement, without retaining a source quote or executable pending receipt.",
    "Core copy borrowing exposes mutable runtime plus immutable generation/input state without revising policy; shared capture, fork copying and restore staging use it. Actual restored-state installation still revises policy.",
    "Portable tests exercise actual snapshot capture/fork and failed staging, original-run and child output parity, exact policy/run identity, and nonrefundable monotone attempts."
  ],
